		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5158&amp;p=37357#p37357"><![CDATA[
If your radio works normally with  S026.057 it's a V5 radio.<br><br>G4EML posted this earlier:<br><br>TYT numbering convention...<br>V0x.xx is for V1 , V2 and V3 radios. (All have identical chipset)<br>V1x.xx is for V4 radios. (Different synthesiser chip)<br>V2x.xx is for V5 radios. (Different synthesiser and IF chips)<br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Tue Jun 03, 2025 9:36 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
